# Documentation loop (thesis-critical)

Everything we do must be tracked in the `docs` repo, continuously (not at the end).
After each step, decision, or experiment, update the relevant artifact:

- **`docs/devlog.md`** — a dated entry per work session/step (newest on top): what we
  did, why, and findings. Link to the ADR/finding it relates to.
- **`docs/decisions/NNNN-*.md`** — one ADR per real decision (context / decision /
  consequences). ADRs are immutable once Accepted; to change course, add a new ADR that
  supersedes the old one — never rewrite an accepted ADR.
- **`docs/findings/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md`** — experiment/analysis write-ups with the concrete
  numbers the thesis will cite (tables preferred).

The `/log-progress` skill automates this loop — prefer it at the end of a step.
